\fs28\b Intelligent Medication Adherence Monitoring System\b0\par
\par
\fs24\b 1. Project Overview\b0\par
\par
- Project name: Intelligent Medication Adherence Monitoring System\par
- What it is: A user-centered solution that helps patients follow their prescribed medication schedules by tracking adherence, providing timely reminders, and notifying caregivers or healthcare providers when doses are missed or patterns of non-adherence appear.\par
- Why it was created: To improve medication adherence, reduce missed or incorrect dosing, support caregivers and clinicians with timely information, and ultimately improve health outcomes for patients who rely on regular medication.\par
- Who benefits: Patients who take regular medications, family members and caregivers who support patients, and healthcare teams that monitor treatment plans and outcomes.\par
\par
\b 2. Goals & Objectives\b0\par
\par
- Improve adherence: Increase the percentage of on-time medication doses taken by patients.\par
- Early intervention: Detect and notify caregivers or healthcare teams about missed doses or concerning patterns quickly.\par
- Reduce caregiver burden: Provide clear, concise alerts and summaries so caregivers can act with confidence.\par
- Enhance safety: Help reduce medication errors by making schedules and reminders easy to follow.\par
- Support engagement: Encourage patients to participate actively in their care by making adherence simple and understandable.\par
\par
\b 3. Feature List (detailed)\b0\par
\par
\bullet  Personalized Reminders\par
\tab - What it does: Sends timely reminders for each scheduled dose and confirms when a dose is taken.\par
\tab - Why it matters: Reduces forgetfulness and helps maintain the correct dosing schedule.\par
\par
\bullet  Adherence Tracking & History\par
\tab - What it does: Records when doses are acknowledged or missed and maintains an easy-to-read history for review.\par
\tab - Why it matters: Provides evidence of adherence over time for caregivers and clinicians to review.\par
\par
\bullet  Alerts & Notifications\par
\tab - What it does: Notifies caregivers or designated contacts when a dose is missed or when repeated non-adherence is detected.\par
\tab - Why it matters: Enables rapid support or intervention to prevent negative health consequences.\par
\par
\bullet  Caregiver Portal / Dashboard\par
\tab - What it does: Presents caregivers with a clear summary of medication schedules, adherence status, recent alerts, and suggested next steps.\par
\tab - Why it matters: Centralizes information so caregivers can prioritize attention and coordinate care.\par
\par
\bullet  Patient Reminders & Acknowledgement\par
\tab - What it does: Lets patients acknowledge they have taken a dose and, if needed, indicate reasons for missed doses.\par
\tab - Why it matters: Encourages patient responsibility while providing context for missed doses.\par
\par
\bullet  Scheduling & Dose Management\par
\tab - What it does: Allows schedules to be created, adjusted, and viewed in a simple calendar-like format.\par
\tab - Why it matters: Keeps complex medication regimens organized and understandable.\par
\par
\bullet  Reports & Summaries\par
\tab - What it does: Generates concise adherence summaries for caregivers and periodic summaries that can be shared with clinicians.\par
\tab - Why it matters: Supports care decisions and helps track progress over time.\par
\par
\bullet  Privacy & Access Controls\par
\tab - What it does: Ensures that patient information and adherence records are visible only to authorized people and that access is managed appropriately.\par
\tab - Why it matters: Protects patient privacy and ensures trust.\par
\par
\b 4. User Roles\b0\par
\par
- Patient\par
\tab - Primary user who receives reminders and acknowledges doses.\par
\tab - Access: View own schedule and adherence history; acknowledge doses; optionally note reasons for missed doses.\par
\par
- Caregiver (Family Member / Home Caregiver)\par
\tab - Supports the patient, receives alerts, and reviews summaries.\par
\tab - Access: View assigned patient schedules and adherence status; receive alerts; view reports; add notes.\par
\par
- Clinician / Healthcare Provider\par
\tab - Monitors adherence trends and acts on clinical concerns.\par
\tab - Access: View adherence reports and summaries for patients under their care; receive periodic summaries or alerts as configured.\par
\par
- System Administrator / Support Staff\par
\tab - Manages user accounts and overall system settings (in a non-technical, administrative sense).\par
\tab - Access: Limited to administrative tasks such as managing contacts and high-level configurations; no alteration of clinical recommendations.\par
\par
\b 5. User Journey / Workflow\b0\par
\par
The following flow describes the typical interactions and escalation paths.\par
\par
1. Patient Enrollment:\par
\tab - Collect patient identity and contact details.\par
\tab - Assign caregiver(s) and emergency contacts.\par
\tab - Enter medication list and schedule (dose, time, frequency).\par
\tab - Confirm activation and notify stakeholders.\par
\par
2. Reminder Delivery:\par
\tab - At scheduled time, send reminder to patient.\par
\tab - Log the reminder event with timestamp.\par
\par
3. Patient Response Handling:\par
\tab - Acknowledge (Taken): record timestamp as successful dose; update adherence history; optional confirmation to caregiver.\par
\tab - Missed (No Acknowledgement): after configured wait time, mark dose as missed; send alert to caregiver; record missed event.\par
\par
4. Caregiver Interaction:\par
\tab - Receive alert; view patient status and recent history; contact patient or assist as needed; mark follow-up actions.\par
\par
5. Escalation Rules:\par
\tab - Single missed dose: caregiver alert and follow-up suggestion.\par
\tab - Multiple consecutive misses or pattern of non-adherence: escalate to clinician with summary report.\par
\par
6. Schedule Adjustment:\par
\tab - Caregiver or clinician updates schedule; system sends update notifications; new schedule becomes active.\par
\par
7. Reporting and Review:\par
\tab - Generate weekly/monthly adherence summaries; caregiver/clinician reviews; decide interventions or schedule changes.\par
\par
\b 6. Module Breakdown\b0\par
\par
- Enrollment & Profile Management: Handles user profiles, contact assignments, and basic preferences.\par
- Scheduling & Reminders: Manages medication schedules and sends reminders at appropriate times.\par
- Adherence Recording: Stores acknowledgements and missed-dose records in an easy-to-read format.\par
- Notifications & Escalation: Manages alert rules, escalation paths, and delivery of notifications to caregivers and clinicians.\par
- Reporting & Summaries: Produces human-readable summaries and periodic reports for caregivers and clinicians.\par
- Access & Privacy Controls: Ensures only authorized individuals can view or act on a patient’s information.\par
- Support & Help: Provides guidance, help content, and contact options for non-technical users.\par
\par
\b 7. Limitations & Future Scope\b0\par
\par
Current Limitations:\par
- The system focuses on reminders and monitoring; it does not replace professional medical advice.\par
- It does not automatically verify ingestion of medication beyond patient acknowledgement.\par
- Integration with external clinical records or pharmacy systems is not included at present.\par
\par
Future Enhancements (possible additions):\par
- Enhanced caregiver collaboration tools such as shared notes and task assignment.\par
- Customizable escalation rules and more flexible alerting preferences.\par
- Optional supportive content for patients (short tips, motivational messages) to encourage adherence.\par
- Safe integration options for clinicians to import adherence summaries into clinical workflows.\par
- Simple tools to support medication reconciliation during transitions of care.\par
\par
\b Appendix — Workflow Diagram (text)\b0\par
\par
Patient Enrollment -> Create Schedule -> Activate Reminders -> Send Reminder -> [Acknowledge: Record] or [No Acknowledge: Wait -> Mark Missed -> Alert Caregiver -> Caregiver Review -> (if repeated) Escalate to Clinician] -> Periodic Summary & Review -> Schedule Update (loop)\par
\par
\par
}\par
